Third-party pieces in the Teddy Rook toolkit, and their licenses

1. d3-geo 3.1.1 and d3-array 3.2.4, by Mike Bostock (ISC License),
   with parts of GeographicLib by Charles Karney (MIT License).
   File: geog/vendor/d3-geo.min.js
   License texts: geog/vendor/LICENSE.txt
   Used by the Geography visuals to draw map projections.

2. Natural Earth map data (public domain), naturalearthdata.com.
   Files: geog/data/*.json (simplified and stored as TopoJSON), and the
   country and state outlines built into geog/viz/geog.js.

3. The language packs, each with its own LICENSE and CREDITS.md:
   greek/        Nestle 1904 Greek New Testament (public domain), MACULA
                 Greek by Clear Bible and Biblica (CC BY 4.0), Dodson Greek
                 Lexicon (public domain). The folder: CC BY 4.0.
   latin/        The Vulgate Gospels as edited in the PROIEL Treebank
                 (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0); William Whitaker's Words (free to copy).
                 The folder: CC BY-NC-SA 3.0.
   classical/    PROIEL Treebank sentences (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0) and Perseus
                 Ancient Greek and Latin Dependency Treebank sentences
                 (CC BY-SA 3.0), in separate files; English from public-domain
                 translations published by the Perseus Digital Library;
                 Liddell-Scott-Jones via Perseus (CC BY-SA 4.0); Whitaker's
                 Words.
   english-kjv/  The King James Version, standard 1769 Oxford text (public
                 domain).
   tools/hieroglyphs/egypt/fonts/  TRB Hieroglyphs (SIL Open Font License
                 1.1) and a subset of GNU FreeFont's FreeSerif (GPL 3 or later
                 with the font exception).
   language-data.js  built from greek/ and english-kjv/ (CC BY 4.0 and public
                 domain).

Everything else in this toolkit is by Teddy Rook: the code under LICENSE
(MIT) and the content under CONTENT-LICENSE (CC BY-NC 4.0). That includes
the Greek alphabet lessons and the cartouche maker in tools/.

